const F=["Earning income|Jobs, freelancing and business income, and how gross pay, deductions and take-home pay differ.","Budgeting|Track income and spending, set limits and goals. Popular methods: 50/30/20, zero-based and envelope budgeting.","Saving|Pay yourself first, automate transfers, start early and stay consistent; small amounts add up fast.","Emergency fund|A cushion of roughly three to six months of essential expenses for job loss or surprise bills.","Credit and credit scores|Pay on time, keep utilization moderate and avoid many new applications; reports and scores shape loan rates.","Borrowing and debt|Understand interest, loan terms and repayments; clear high-interest debt first (avalanche) or smallest first (snowball).","Credit cards|Pay the full statement balance every month to avoid interest; know the fees, limits and reward traps.","Investing|Stocks, bonds, mutual funds, index funds and real estate; match choices to your goals and risk tolerance.","Compound interest|Returns that earn their own returns, which is why starting early matters. Try the calculator below.","Risk and diversification|Spread money across assets; higher potential returns come with higher risk.","Retirement planning|Start early, use tax-advantaged retirement accounts and estimate what you will need later.","Insurance and protection|Health, life, vehicle and property cover transfer big financial risks to an insurer.","Taxes|Income tax basics, deductions, filing deadlines and keeping good records.","Inflation|Rising prices erode cash over time, so saving alone is rarely enough for long-term goals.","Buying goods and services|Compare total cost, separate needs from wants and spot marketing tricks.","Scams and fraud|Phishing, fake investment schemes and OTP fraud: never share passwords or OTPs, and verify before paying.","Financial goals|Set short-, medium- and long-term goals for education, a home or a business, and review them yearly."];
