const DEEP={"chemistry/0.1":"Atoms bond to reach a stable outer shell, usually eight electrons. Metals tend to lose electrons and nonmetals to gain them, so they form ionic bonds, an attraction between oppositely charged ions. Two nonmetals share electrons in covalent bonds, which can be single, double or triple. In metals, electrons move freely between atoms, giving conductivity and shine.|Sodium gives one electron to chlorine, making Na⁺ and Cl⁻ that lock into table salt. In water (H₂O), oxygen shares one electron pair with each hydrogen. Electronegativity difference tells you the type: above about 1.7 is ionic, 0.4 to 1.7 is polar covalent, below 0.4 is nonpolar.|Do not think of ionic and covalent as two sealed boxes: it is a spectrum. Draw dot diagrams to count electrons before guessing a bond.",
"chemistry/0.6":"Brønsted–Lowry acids donate H⁺ and bases accept it. pH = −log[H⁺], so a drop of one pH unit means ten times more H⁺. Strong acids such as HCl ionize fully in water, while weak acids such as acetic acid only partly. A buffer is a weak acid with its conjugate base and resists pH change.|A 0.01 M HCl solution has [H⁺] = 10⁻² so pH = 2. Lemon juice is about pH 2, pure water 7, baking soda solution about 8.3 and bleach about 12.5. Titrating 25 mL of HCl with 0.10 M NaOH that needs 20 mL shows the acid is 0.080 M.|Strong does not mean concentrated. Always add acid to water, never water to acid, and wear eye protection.",
"chemistry/0.8":"Oxidation is loss of electrons and reduction is gain (OIL RIG). Oxidation states track where electrons go. The oxidizer is reduced and the reducer is oxidized, and the two half-reactions always happen together. In a galvanic cell the electron flow between them is used as electric current.|Iron rusting: 4Fe + 3O₂ + water gives Fe₂O₃·nH₂O; iron goes from 0 to +3 (oxidized) while oxygen goes from 0 to −2 (reduced). In a Zn–Cu cell, zinc dissolves and copper deposits, giving about 1.10 V.|Count electrons on both sides when balancing, and remember that a substance cannot be oxidized unless something else is reduced."};
